  "id": "generalizability-theory",
  "term": "generalizability theory",
  "definition": "Generalizability theory is a statistical approach to evaluating how reliable a measurement is in the behavioral sciences. It examines several possible sources of measurement error at the same time and estimates how much each testing condition or factor contributes to score variation across acceptable observations.",
